Welcome to World 6: Problems!

This is it. The grand finale of the Number Theory Game.

You've built a massive toolkit of abstract theorems. You've conquered the Chinese Remainder Theorem and relaxed with the divisibility rules. But math isn't just about abstract variables like $a$, $b$, and $m$. It's about solving real problems.

In this final world, we will use your theorems to crush concrete numerical problems that would be too massive to compute directly. You'll see how abstract algebra gives you elegant shortcuts to the right answers. Let's put your theory to the ultimate test!
